From 8c3c3bafc2efef597973fd24610f148631779747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claudius <claudiusthebot@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] starlte: DWC3 CDC-ACM gadget console (usb_gadget) and
 MAX77705 USB switch close, with the log tap and a 'return' command

The kernel's console ring streamed to a host over a CDC-ACM serial port on the S9's USB-C (/dev/cu.usbmodem* on macOS), and a
line console back; 'return' flushes the log and resets into recovery. Uses Scion's hakios DWC3 gadget (hakios.dwc3.c,
hakios.exynos_usb.c, hakios.usb_acm.h; drivers/usb), the Exynos HSI2C master and the MUIC sequence of hakios.max77705.c to close
the USB-C switch (starlte_muic.c). starlte_usbcon.c supplies what those drivers need from their kernel and the tap fed from the
a5xelte console ring. Boot-args usb_gadget=N, usb_muic.
